-- title:
--   Valuative criterion over a DVR for the full-level moduli ring
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes and $M'$ a nonzero natural number, with $\ell \ge 3$ and with $\ell$, $M'$, $2$ and $3$ units in $A$. Assume the two equivariance hypotheses that, over every $A$-algebra $T$, a level-$\ell$ datum $D$ (four coordinates $x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q$) satisfying `IsLevelPStructure` for a Weierstrass curve $W$ transports along a variable change $C$ to `D.variableChange C` for $C \bullet W$, and that a polynomial $h$ with `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` transports to `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h` for $C \bullet W$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the graded projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A$-algebras, assumed chord–tangent (on points over fields it induces the addition of the affine curve and is Galois-equivariant) and origin-normalised (its identity section is given by a chart homomorphism killing $x/y$ and $z/y$), and let $\mathcal{T}$ be a level transport for $\mathcal{G}$ and $q$ on raw Drinfeld pairs, compatible with sections under variable change and coefficient change. Assume further that every variable change and every coefficient change of a projective Weierstrass curve is realised by a graded ring homomorphism of projective-model gradings satisfying the irrelevant-ideal condition, i.e. by a map satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`. Let $P_0$ be an abstract moduli package for the level moduli datum attached to `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q`, whose points over an $A$-algebra $T$ are variable-change orbits of tuples consisting of a Weierstrass curve over $T$ with unit discriminant, a $\Gamma_0$-type kernel polynomial for each prime power dividing $M'$, a level-$\ell$ datum, and a Drinfeld $q$-basis pair; thus $P_0$ consists of an $A$-algebra $B_0$, a universal point over $B_0$, and the property that every point over every $A$-algebra $T$ is `map φ` of the universal point for a unique $A$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : B_0 \to T$. Finally let $K$ be a field which is an $A$-algebra, $V \subseteq K$ a valuation subring that is a discrete valuation ring, assume $\operatorname{algebraMap} A K$ lands in $V$, and let $\varphi : B_0 \to K$ be an $A$-algebra homomorphism with $\varphi(j_0) \in V$, where $j_0 \in B_0$ is the $j$-invariant of the universal point. Then $\varphi(b) \in V$ for every $b \in B_0$.
--
--   This is the valuative criterion, in the discrete-valuation case, for the coordinate ring of the full-level moduli problem over the $j$-line: integrality of the image of $j_0$ forces integrality of the whole image. It feeds the statement that $B_0$ is integral over the subalgebra generated by $j_0$, and thence the finiteness results for the full-level moduli ring.
